WEBVTT

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:46.990
<b>Ghosts Aren't the Only Ones 
Who Run Wild Around Graveyards</b>

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.530
Boss!

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.240
You really sure about this?

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.230
If one faction causes trouble,

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.900
the other three gang up to crush it?

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.250
It's obvious that they 
want to get rid of us!

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.410
I'd say that this saves time.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.700
This is a chance to show them who the

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.590
real king of the Kabuki District is.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.220
But that means we'll have 
to deal with Otose...

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.500
My memory's been getting worse.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.220
Who is this Otose person?

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.110
Idiot!

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.700
We're not supposed to mention the hag

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.030
while the boss is around!

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.890
The vixen is not as much 
of a concern as the cub.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.990
Focus on him.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.300
Damn.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.990
What is that kid doing?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.700
You were dancing to her tune.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.370
That's not like you.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.540
Kada is using you to get rid of Jirocho,

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.380
who's hurting her business.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.530
I just want to live peacefully

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.740
in this town with my comrades.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.470
I'll dance a waltz or octopus 
dance if that's what it takes.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.410
So you can clean up this 
town by eliminating him?

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.220
Even if that were true,

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.930
I could never bring 
myself to love a town

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.480
that's neat and tidy.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.750
Spoken like a true trashy old hag.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.840
I believe that you're old friends

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.110
with the trashy old geezer?

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.560
Haven't talked to him in over ten years.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.680
Doesn't really matter if a 
dangerous old man dies or not.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:13.620
But...

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.000
<i>I'm here to turn the town </i>

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.770
<i>where Jirocho is into a garden.</i>

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.370
The timing's too perfect.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:24.690
Finally, it's time for payback.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.670
Like I said before,

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.630
I always return the 
favor, seven for three.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.230
Nobody parts their hair 7:3 anymore.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.810
You should shave your head

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.740
and opt for the bald look.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:37.780
Up yours!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:41.300
My hair is styled like Joe Odagiri!

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.400
Fashion trends come back in a cycle!

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.380
Hold on here.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.670
I was egged on by this stupid girl.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.100
I have no grudge against you, Joe Schmo.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.780
Who are you calling Joe Schmo?!

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.030
Besides, that's not what 
my boy here told me.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.540
I know what's going down.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.580
You promised to

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.710
help her decorate our 
boss with red flowers.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.040
How do you know that?

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.910
Why don't you tell him what you really

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.290
mean when you say red 
flowers, Pirako-han?

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.110
Uh, Pirako-chan?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.860
U-Uh, are you...

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.850
Bro, my boss was

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.800
a relative of Jirocho, 
and an old friend.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.360
He used to tell me when I was young,

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:25.060
about the great Jirocho, 
warrior among warriors.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.160
The warriors you see around these days

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.870
are just a bunch of wild hotheads.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.070
But he was different.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.210
He would save the weak 
and crush the strong.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:36.810
He would only employ his strength

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.700
for the sake of his particular justice.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.830
That's what you call a true warrior.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.670
That's too hard for me to understand.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.640
Sorry about that.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.970
The more I talk, the less sense I make.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.220
Basically, Jirocho was a flowery man.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:59.620
That's probably what 
drew your mother to him.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:03.830
Though the flowers in him 
died at some point...

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.380
He abandoned his wife and child,

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.270
and crushed his wife's 
family because of business.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.040
And now he's picking a stupid fight

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.270
with a tranny and an old hag.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:23.820
I just want to see the old 
Jirocho one more time.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.760
To help him take the world...

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.560
To help make some pretty 
flowers bloom in my old man.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.690
Huh? What's she talking about?

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.110
That went completely over my head.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.090
What? What?!

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.790
There you have it.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:40.790
Pirako-han is...

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.330
No, the young lady is

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.100
Jirocho's daughter!

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:47.480
To be precise, she's the daughter of the

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.460
missus who divorced the boss 
and went back to her family.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:50.660
Bullshit!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.090
Help your old man take the world?!

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:54.740
That's the complete opposite of revenge!

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:57.270
Isn't that what I said?

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.960
I'm here to decorate him with flowers.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.100
You were talking about making 
me the big boss of Japan!

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:04.420
You were trying to 
make me fight Jirocho!

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:09.350
Yakuza grow stronger by recruiting 
the people they beat.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:11.700
My old man can take the 
world if the strongest

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.650
man in the Kabuki 
district is on his side.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.330
Once you're the big boss,

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.260
my old man will be the big, big boss!

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.040
Young lady, it's settled.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:24.440
Bro, the Jirocho gang will 
be making their move now.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:26.520
Do you know what's happened?

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.600
There's a law in this lawless town now.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:32.080
If any faction starts a fight,

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.820
the other Devas will crush them.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.280
The first victim will probably be

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.080
the boss of a certain someone

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.840
who picked a fight with the Jirocho gang

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.810
over a helpless little girl, Otose.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.940
But it's your call to make, Bro.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.410
Please join us!

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:51.410
Or else we'll have to 
drop you in the ocean,

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.920
and Otose will be targeted by 
everyone in the Kabuki district!

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:58.140
Hey, I'm guessing that's 
supposed to be a threat,

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.700
but if you kill me here,

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:02.260
you'll be considered the aggressors.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.400
You an idiot?

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.330
Why do you think we put on a show

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.150
in the middle of town?!

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:09.890
We got plenty of witnesses!

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:11.580
You're the idiots!

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.330
The Four Devas aren't gonna 
move because of a little spat!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:17.020
A death is far more serious!

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:17.750
Die, baldie!

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.000
Go bald down your parted hair line!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:19.860
Go bald all over your body!

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:20.700
I ain't gonna go bald!

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.930
Every week, I part my 
hair to the opposite side

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:25.410
to avoid excessive damage to my scalp!

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.950
I ain't like Sanshi Katsura!

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:33.160
If that's not enough, how's this?

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.400
We'll say that you killed 
our young leader here,

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.260
and we killed you for revenge.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.660
Huh? No way...

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.350
Bro!

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:49.560
Is your boss the guy 
with the parted hair?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.070
Or is it Jirocho?

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.050
B-But...

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:55.110
If you move, I'll turn 
you all into flowers.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.230
Got it, Bro?

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.610
I'm serious.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.620
D-Damn you!

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:09.230
Bastard!

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:10.960
He jumped into the water 
with the concrete!

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.460
Is he trying to escape?!

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:13.630
Nope.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.180
He went to save him.

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:16.840
That's stupid!

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:17.880
He can't move!

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:19.000
And why would he save Bro?!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.970
Yes, he's stupid.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:24.210
I was very surprised.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:28.260
But that's why I wanted him on our side.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.730
But he also chose the old hag.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.570
Pity.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.010
Bye-bye, Bro.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.770
Pity.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:42.840
I came up with this 
plan so the three of us

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.530
could deal with Jirocho,

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:47.370
but I never would have 
expected Otose to...

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.160
Don't be ridiculous!

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.700
Otose-san would never...

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.910
Pako would never do anything like that!

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:56.530
We know how gentle they are!

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:58.040
Calm down, Assmi!

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:58.960
Don't call me Assmi!

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.120
It's Azumi, damn it!

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.550
Shut the hell up, Ass!

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:05.480
Could you add the "mi"?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.020
You can call me Assmi as 
long as the "mi" is there.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:13.060
It looks like we were the only ones

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:16.060
serious about stopping this conflict.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.820
When did you make a deal with Jirocho?

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.820
You think I would make 
a deal with that vixen?

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.330
Were you pushed by the kid?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.580
No, were you the one who pushed the kid?

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:32.800
Don't play dumb!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:36.310
They might be rotten to the core,

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.420
but they aren't dirty like you people!

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.060
That's enough.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.310
You should stop that, Saigo-san.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.420
It's not nice to whine 
and go back on your word.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:46.430
Pleasure to meet you.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:50.180
I'm Jirocho's daughter, Pirako Doromizu.

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:53.280
Jirocho's...

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.240
I have a question for you, Saigo-san.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.230
Do you have any

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:00.020
proof that Otose-san 
hasn't done anything?

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:03.350
My proof is the fact 
that you have no proof.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:07.030
Why would Otose pick 
a fight with Jirocho?

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.450
And now of all times?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.410
There's obviously a conspiracy going on.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.750
Nobody would spend that

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.240
much effort to kill an old hag.

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:18.690
Besides, we have proof

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.920
that Otose-san would pick 
a fight with my old man.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:25.170
There's a long history between them.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:27.170
Isn't that right, old man?

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.090
Here it is.

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:32.000
Otose-san's husband, Tatsugoro Terada,

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.930
was killed by my old man.

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:40.880
Oh? You didn't know?

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.820
What about this?

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.120
My old man and Tatsugoro-san

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.440
were friends when they were young.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:51.320
But then they got into a 
fight over a certain girl.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.160
Tatsugoro-san was the 
one who won her over.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:57.880
I'm sure that my old man 
wasn't happy about it.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.130
Stop it...

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.430
That's why he killed his old friend.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.960
So he could have the girl.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:04.340
Stop it.

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:07.070
Do you know why he abandoned his own

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:09.840
wife and daughter to come to this town?

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:14.770
That's because the girl, 
Otose-san, is here.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.020
Didn't you hear me say to stop?

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:23.520
See? It's just like I said.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:26.940
He cares more about Otose-san 
than his own daughter.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:32.310
You came here just to tell me that?

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.580
Such a dutiful daughter.

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:36.730
If what I'm saying isn't true,

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:39.280
that should mean you can kill Otose-san.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.420
Are you running away?!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.210
Saigo, don't worry.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:55.830
Yakuza don't need trannies 
to clean up their mess.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.070
You stay out of it.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.480
I'll settle this myself.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:01.800
Wait!

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:02.860
I'm not done talking...

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:08.990
I'll spare you this one time, 
since you kept whining.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.950
Could you shut up now?

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.260
How am I supposed to shut u--

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:14.950
Have you forgotten?

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.160
If you go back on your word,

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:19.450
we'll have to eliminate you as well.

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:21.750
When laying siege to a castle,

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:24.150
what would you target first?

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.030
The weakest spot in the wall.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.960
A seasoned soldier like yourself 
should be aware of this.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.970
M-Mama!

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.970
Te-Teru-kun is... Teru-kun is...!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.580
Damn you!

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:41.730
<b>Snack Otose</b>

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:41.730
I see.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:43.730
Very well.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:49.080
Don't worry.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:50.570
That was Gintoki.

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.800
It seems that Pirako is safe.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:55.250
They learned about the 
new rule right before

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.450
they were about to take 
on Jirocho's gang.

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:00.490
Apparently, they were able 
to talk things through.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.070
That's a relief.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:04.080
I was worried that we would be too late.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:05.570
They kept us worried this whole time.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:07.250
What are they doing?!

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:09.640
I appreciate everything you've done.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.890
You haven't eaten since 
yesterday, right?

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:14.360
Now that you mention it, I'm starting 
to feel hungry now that everything's okay.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.430
Want to grab something to eat?

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:16.260
Can we?

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:17.340
Yakiniku!

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.480
We must have yakiniku!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.450
At a really expensive place!

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:20.170
Stupid!

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.550
That won't fill my stomach!

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:22.320
A buffet!

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.800
At a place with ice cream!

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.400
Stop fighting.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.520
Let's compromise by 
going to a gas station.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:29.040
How is that a compromise?!

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.760
Go on ahead.

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:34.030
I'll join you once Gintoki 
and Pirako are back.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:36.640
Please hurry.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.160
We'll wait for you 
before we start eating.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.850
But the ice cream doesn't count, right?

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.910
I can eat ice cream while 
we're waiting, right?

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.790
Didn't Otose-san seem a little strange?

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.070
How?

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:51.470
When she offers to buy someone dinner,

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.550
there's usually a catch.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.880
No, that's not what I meant...

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:57.300
Oh, sorry.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.610
He's covered in blood!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:00.330
Sorry!

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.230
Is this my fault?!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.310
Is this my fault?!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:03.600
Huh?

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:04.810
It's Katsuo-san...

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:07.810
Hey! The bucket that 
just ran past us...!

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:25.950
Gran!

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:40.970
<b>Terada Family Grave</b>

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.970
It's rare to see you here.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.970
I'm assuming that you brought flowers.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:42.720
Hell no.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.480
Did you want me to bring 
flowers for you, Otose?

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:50.360
It's been years since 
you've spoken to me,

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.010
and that's all you have to say?

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.980
You never change.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.420
If you lay me to rest 
next to my husband,

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.260
I suppose I can't complain.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.990
I heard that you took care of my kid.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:07.270
Save your thanks for that idiot.

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:11.830
Though apparently, that 
kid of yours got him good.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:14.270
She's quite a dutiful daughter.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:16.620
She came all the way here to clean

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.520
this town for the sake of a

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.380
stupid father who abandoned her.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:25.120
We've both been dancing to 
the tune of a little kid.

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.520
The years haven't been kind to us.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:31.150
Well, I suppose you knew 
what was happening.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.330
The villain Jirocho

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:36.650
can't go against the 
daughter he left in tears?

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.650
Otose...

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.590
Get out of this town.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:44.190
This place will become 
a battlefield very soon.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:47.980
It was gonna happen even if my 
kid didn't rush things along.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:51.490
You'll only get in the way if you stay.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:55.800
So you were planning on 
starting a war, period.

00:15:55.170 --> 00:16:00.420
<b>Terada Family Grave</b>

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:57.250
I would have hoped that

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.220
you wouldn't say those 
words in his presence,

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:00.420
even as a joke.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.240
Policeman and vigilante.

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:06.600
The two of you were both 
protecting this town,

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:08.150
despite your different positions,

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:10.480
but I suppose that was in the past.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.260
Jirocho.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:18.190
You went so far as to 
abandon your wife and child

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.670
so you could do this?

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.870
Times have changed.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:30.940
A vigilante can't protect anything.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:35.310
He died and left you behind.

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.350
Your methods are old-fashioned.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:41.390
You're just a nuisance,

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.600
both you and Tatsugoro.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:46.140
This town doesn't need you anymore.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:50.640
This town belongs to me.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.730
I'll give you one more chance.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.770
Get out of this town.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:01.650
I have a favor to ask.

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:05.650
They call me one of the Four Devas,

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:09.450
but I don't have any 
members in my faction.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:12.960
<b>I'm sick of waiting for you to pay the rent. Take your fools and scram. Never come back to this town.
--Otose</b>

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.960
My life is all you need.

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.750
They serve no use at all.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:20.100
They just happen to be my family.

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:25.710
Is that your answer?

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:11.140
You're Gintoki?

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.280
You were a step too late.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.640
I buried her with her husband.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:19.650
Funny how it works.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.270
I believe that you were serving as her

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:25.780
bodyguard to pay back a debt?

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:29.160
That's over now. Your job is done.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.590
Scram.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.410
I'll spare your life for her sake.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.200
Ouch...

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.170
The hell was that?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.890
Not bad, kid.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:52.640
You made me draw my sword.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:58.140
But are you willing to let Otose's 
efforts to save your lives...

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:00.940
...go to waste?

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:19.830
You're not being very reasonable.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.010
It's over.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:47.190
I heard that Otose was keeping 
a crazy monster around.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.340
So you're the White Yaksha?

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.230
I never knew there was a freak like 
you following in my footsteps.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:53.950
However...

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:55.480
A generation managed

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:58.450
to survive the brutal 
battles of the Joi war.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:01.780
There were plenty more 
like you out there.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.370
Get lost, watchdog.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:09.690
There's nothing for you to protect here.

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.050
Hey, Gran.

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:57.290
Are those manju?

00:20:57.850 --> 00:20:59.020
Can I have some?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.560
I'm starving to death here.

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.990
These belong to my husband.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.560
Ask him.

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:18.200
What did my husband say?

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:19.980
Beats me.

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:21.700
The dead don't talk.

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:23.970
You're just asking for it.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:26.210
Don't blame me if you get cursed.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:34.310
The dead don't talk and 
they don't eat dango.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:36.720
So I made a one-sided promise.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.270
I won't forget this debt.

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:47.310
Your wife doesn't have 
that much longer to live,

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:52.720
but I'm going to protect 
her in your stead.

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:01.410
Gran...

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:44.970
<b>Next Episode
Chains of a Warrior</b>
